    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nstarter.mini\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello, thanks for this very nice set of plugins !\r\n\r\nIn `lua/mini/starter.lua:1389`, some keymaps are hard-coded and overwrite some of mine (namely 'M-j' and 'M-k', which I use to navigate between windows, so I am \"stuck\" in any starter.mini window):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nbuf_keymap('<Up>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('prev')]])\r\nbuf_keymap('<C-p>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('prev')]])\r\nbuf_keymap('<M-k>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('prev')]])\r\nbuf_keymap('<Down>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('next')]])\r\nbuf_keymap('<C-n>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('next')]])\r\nbuf_keymap('<M-j>', [[MiniStarter.update_current_item('next')]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nCould there be a way to detect that these keymaps are in use and not overwrite them ? Or maybe give an optional possibility to not set any keymaps when loading starter.mini ?\r\n\r\nThanks in advance for your time spent reading this.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-2324+g4948fa42e\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. launch `nvim` with a keymap set for \"M-j\" in normal mode and load `mini.starter`\r\n2. invoke `MiniStarter.open()`\r\n3. press `<M-j>`\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n`nvim` should do whatever was initially mapped to \"M-j\" (in my case I would like to switch to another window in nvim)\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n`nvim` goes one entry down in starter.mini window",
