            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nAs 'mini.starter' has quite a big config already and was done quite a long time ago, it does not have designated `mappings` option for buffer local mappings. And I am hesitant about adding one.\r\n\r\nWhat I would suggest doing is to override those buffer-local mappings inside Starter buffer:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.starter').setup()\r\nlocal override_mappings = function(args)\r\n  vim.keymap.set('n', '<M-j>', '<Cmd>wincmd j<CR>', { buffer = args.buf })\r\n  vim.keymap.set('n', '<M-k>', '<Cmd>wincmd k<CR>', { buffer = args.buf })\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniStarterOpened', callback = override_mappings })\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr perhaps a more robust solution would be to delete them (buffer-local mappings, that is):\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.starter').setup()\r\nlocal delete_extra_mappings = function(args)\r\n  vim.keymap.del('n', '<M-j>', { buffer = args.buf })\r\n  vim.keymap.del('n', '<M-k>', { buffer = args.buf })\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniStarterOpened', callback = delete_extra_mappings })\r\n```\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
