            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Is there no need to create an autogroup in case mini.starter is run more than once per nvim session?\r\n\r\nSure, wrapping in augroup is a cleaner approach.\r\n\r\nJust to be clear, though: this does not have to depend whether `MiniStarter.open()` is run more than once per session, but whether the `vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd()` can be run more than once. As usually it is run once per session, it is fine for this example. But again, if you might resource config during same session, wrapping in augroup is better.",
